**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
.env
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Filled-in variable files. Every terraform.tfvars.example in this repo says
# "copy to terraform.tfvars and fill in", and the filled-in copy is account
# identifiers and sometimes secrets. A rule beats the comment that used to ask
# people not to commit it.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example

# Saved plans. A plan file contains the *resolved* values of every attribute,
# including the secrets a variable or data source pulled in — it is closer to a
# credential dump than to a diff.
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json
plan.out
plan.json

# Terraform override files are a local-only mechanism by design: they silently
# replace blocks in the surrounding configuration. Committed to a branch that a
# Space-admin stack executes, an override.tf is a way to change what runs while
# leaving main.tf looking untouched in review.
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Local tool caches and scanner output. CI writes these into the workspace, and
# so does anyone running the same commands locally.
.tflint.d/
*.sarif
hygiene.json
.venv/
venv/

# cartogopher local artifacts
bakes/
fast.yaml

.DS_Store
